      "writtenOn": "2025-12-02T03:15:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I added it locally and tried having FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_ELANI80SA select the read-mode option. However, during build I hit warnings that select has no effect on choice symbols, which then causes the build to fail. The warnings look like:\n```\nwarning: the choice symbol FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_ELAN80SERIES_READ_LINEWISE (defined at /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/Kconfig.elan:46) is selected by the following symbols, but select/imply has no effect on choice symbols\n - FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_ELANI80SA (defined at /mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/Kconfig.elan:65)\nerror: Aborting due to Kconfig warnings\n```\nSo it seems select cannot be used on items inside a choice, which is why I wasn’t able to make the sensor config select the read mode.",
